From: PX4 Development Team <px4@px4.io>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] armv8-m: declare r0 clobbered in exception_direct FPU asm

The inline asm writes r0 before vmsr fpscr; without the clobber the
compiler keeps the IRQ number in r0 and every interrupt dispatches as
0x40000 -> irq_unexpected_isr -> PANIC. Backport of upstream apache/nuttx
master arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_doirq.c.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_doirq.c b/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_doirq.c
index a86de9f7e7..5f902b1eda 100644
--- a/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_doirq.c
+++ b/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_doirq.c
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@ void exception_direct(void)
       "vmsr fpscr, r0\n"
       :
       : "i" (ARMV8M_FPSCR_LTPSIZE_NONE)
+      : "r0"
     );
 #endif
 
